defmodule <%= inspect(@module) %> do
  @moduledoc """
  Signing people in to the application's pages through EHOS: `EhOsContract.Auth.SignIn`,
  started where `config :eh_os_contract_auth, :sign_in` is set, which `config/runtime.exs`
  does in a release from what EHOS gives the application.

  There is no EHOS to sign in with in development or in tests, so nothing is started
  there. In tests `/auth/ehos/sign-in` answers 503, as it does while EHOS cannot be reached, and
  a page behind the router's `:signed_in` pipeline sends the browser to it. In development, where
  `config/dev.exs` turns on the development mode of `eh_os_contract_auth`, both send the browser
  to `/dev/sign-in`, where `EhOsContract.Auth.Development` signs a person in with a key of its
  own; with the mode off, `/auth/ehos/sign-in` answers 503 there too. In tests, and in
  development with the mode off, a callback or a sign-out raises, since no client holds what
  they need. A release whose `ehos.yaml` declares no `sign_in` starts nothing either, and signs
  nobody in, even where EHOS gives it a key to read the people or send mail with.
  """

  @doc false
  @spec child_spec(keyword()) :: Supervisor.child_spec()
  def child_spec(opts) do
    if Application.get_env(:eh_os_contract_auth, :sign_in) do
      EhOsContract.Auth.SignIn.child_spec(opts)
    else
      %{id: EhOsContract.Auth.SignIn, start: {__MODULE__, :start_link, [opts]}}
    end
  end

  @doc false
  @spec start_link(keyword()) :: :ignore
  def start_link(_opts), do: :ignore
end
